WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.377
Start with the selected website, then choose a period such as today or the last 24 hours.

00:00:07.377 --> 00:00:12.941
Use the interval menu to group activity by hour or another available granularity.

00:00:12.941 --> 00:00:19.361
Compare periods only after the report has data; zero means no matching visits were recorded.

00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:27.979
Use channel, referrer, campaign, page, entry page, browser, operating system, and device panels to narrow the same time window.

00:00:27.979 --> 00:00:31.080
Selecting a row adds a report filter.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.953
Remove the active filter to return to the full site view.

00:00:36.153 --> 00:00:38.808
Realtime activity updates as events arrive.

00:00:38.808 --> 00:00:45.002
Country aggregates are available only when a trusted hosting proxy provides a country code.

00:00:45.002 --> 00:00:51.638
The report does not request browser GPS and does not claim an exact person's location.

00:00:51.638 --> 00:00:56.504
If the map is empty, check whether geo headers are configured.

00:00:56.704 --> 00:01:02.617
A share link can expose the selected public report to anyone who receives it.

00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:05.996
Check the date range and filters before sharing.

00:01:05.996 --> 00:01:12.331
Keep private account pages and server keys out of public links, posts, screenshots, and videos.
